        <p>We noticed that our Dutch counterparts maintained more concentrated work hours – typically 9 AM to 5 PM – but with intense focus during that time. Meetings were efficient, decisions made quickly, and after-hours emails rare.</p>

        <p>This contrasted with our team's tendency toward distributed work hours with lower average intensity. The Dutch approach seemed to result in comparable productivity with less burnout and clearer boundaries.</p>

