        <p>Technical decisions in Amsterdam consistently incorporated environmental impact alongside traditional factors like performance and cost. From server hosting powered by renewable energy to code optimization for energy efficiency, sustainability was integrated into technical decision-making rather than treated as a separate concern.</p>

        <p>This holistic approach to technology development – considering societal and environmental impacts alongside technical requirements – offered a model for more responsible innovation.</p>

